<header><p class="st-kicker">protectorate · Balkans and Hungary</p><h1 class="st-title">Albanian Kingdom (1943-1944)</h1><p class="st-meta">1943 CE – 1944 CE · capital Tirana</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Nominally independent Albanian state set up by Germany after Italy's surrender in 1943, which kept Kosovo but was defeated by the Communist Partisans.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>When <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> capitulated in September 1943, German troops occupied the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/albanian-kingdom-1939-1943">Albanian Kingdom</a> (1939-1943). Seeking local support, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> declared <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/albania">Albania</a> independent, convened a national assembly and set up a Regency Council headed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mehdi-frasheri">Mehdi Frashëri</a>, with Albanian governments led successively by figures such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rexhep-mitrovica">Rexhep Mitrovica</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The regime claimed neutrality and kept the Albanian-inhabited lands of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kosovo">Kosovo</a> and western Macedonia added in 1941, while <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> controlled the military situation. Some nationalists of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balli-kombetar">Balli Kombëtar</a> cooperated with the Germans against the Partisans, and an SS division was recruited in Kosovo. Many <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jews">Jews</a> in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/albania">Albania</a> were sheltered by Albanian families and survived.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/enver-hoxha">Enver Hoxha's</a> Partisans won the civil war and took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tirana">Tirana</a> on 17 November 1944 as German forces withdrew. The communists then founded what became the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/peoples-socialist-republic-of-albania">People's Socialist Republic of Albania</a>, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kosovo">Kosovo</a> returned to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yugoslavia">Yugoslavia</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/albanian-kingdom-1943-1944.jpg" alt="Albanian Kingdom (1943-1944)" width="320" height="160"><figcaption>Image: SeNeKa · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Albania_(1943%E2%80%931944).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1943 CE – 1944 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>protectorate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Tirana</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Mehdi Frashëri, Rexhep Mitrovica</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam, Orthodox and Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Albanian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/albania">Albania</a>, <a href="/countries/kosovo">Kosovo</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>German-occupied Albania</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1944&amp;focus=albanian-kingdom-1943-1944" aria-label="Albanian Kingdom (1943-1944) on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5164 704 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Albanian Kingdom (1943-1944) lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5484 960L5484 960M5484 960L5300 622M5484 960L5484 960"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5484 960h0M5300 622h0M5484 960h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5484 960h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5484 960h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Tirana. <a href="/atlas?year=1944&amp;focus=albanian-kingdom-1943-1944">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
